My apologies. You were clear, and I over-delivered by including the table-level comments.
Here are the exact SQL scripts containing only the column comments for those three tables, ready for your UAT deployment.
1. MASTER_JOURNAL
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.JOURNAL_ID IS 'Unique sequential identifier for the master journal entry.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.JOURNAL_AMT IS 'Absolute transaction amount. Always positive; Txn Type determines debit/credit.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.AR_FLAG IS 'Status flag indicating the record state. Default is A for Approved/Active.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.BATCH_ID IS 'Reference to the parent batch from JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.JOURNAL_BRANCH IS 'The branch code where the transaction is booked.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.JOURNAL_CGL IS 'The 10-digit Common General Ledger (CGL) account code.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.COMMON_BATCH_REMARKS IS 'Batch-level remarks provided by the executor during approval.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.CURRENCY IS 'The 3-character currency code (e.g., INR, USD) for the transaction.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.JOURNAL_ID_REF IS 'Reference back to the original row ID from the JOURNAL_REQUEST staging table.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.JOURNAL_PDATE IS 'The posting date or CSV date of the journal entry.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.PRODUCT_TYPE IS 'The 8-digit product classification code, or A for default.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.REMARKS IS 'Line-level narration or specific remarks for this individual entry.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN MASTER_JOURNAL.TXN_TYPE IS 'Specifies if the entry is a Debit or Credit.';

2. JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.BATCH_ID IS 'Primary Key. Unique identifier for the uploaded batch file.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.CREATOR_ID IS 'User ID of the person who uploaded and initiated the batch.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.REQ_DATE IS 'Timestamp when the batch was originally requested/uploaded.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.BATCH_REMARKS IS 'Initial remarks provided by the creator upon upload.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.TOTAL_ROWS IS 'Total number of valid transaction rows contained in this batch.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.TOTAL_DEBIT IS 'Sum of all debit transaction amounts in the batch.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.TOTAL_CREDIT IS 'Sum of all credit transaction amounts in the batch.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.BATCH_STATUS IS 'Current workflow state (e.g., PENDING, ACCEPTED, REJECTED, ERROR).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.EXECUTOR_ID IS 'User ID of the person who approved or rejected the batch.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.EXECUTION_DATE IS 'Timestamp when the batch was approved or rejected.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.EXECUTOR_REMARKS IS 'Remarks provided by the executor when approving or rejecting.';

3. JOURNAL_REQUEST
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.JOURNAL_ID IS 'Primary Key. Unique identifier for the individual staging request row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.BATCH_ID IS 'Foreign key linking this row to its parent in JOURNAL_BATCH_MASTER.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.REQ_CSV_DATE IS 'The transaction date provided in the uploaded file.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.REQ_BRANCH_CODE IS 'The branch code requested for the transaction.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.REQ_CURRENCY IS 'The 3-character currency code requested.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.REQ_CGL IS 'The 10-digit CGL account code requested.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.REQ_AMOUNT IS 'Raw requested amount (can be positive for debit or negative for credit).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.REQ_NARRATION IS 'Line-level remarks or narration from the uploaded file.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.REQ_PRODUCT IS 'The product classification code requested.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.COMMON_BATCH_REMARKS IS 'Remarks inherited from the batch creation process.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.REQ_STATUS IS 'Row-level processing status (e.g., P for Pending, A for Approved, R for Rejected).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.EXECUTOR_ID IS 'User ID of the person who processed this specific row.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.EXECUTION_DATE IS 'Timestamp when this specific row was processed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN JOURNAL_REQUEST.EXECUTOR_REMARKS IS 'Remarks provided by the executor applied to this specific row.';

